# MRL family 9: capture-group spans alongside MRL pruning.
#
# Half the promise ("no answer changes, ever") is about capture spans, not
# just the overall match span. These reuse shapes from earlier families
# (nested quantifiers, alternation, near-minimum subjects) with real
# capturing groups so a bound that quietly moves where a repetition
# lands -- without changing the OVERALL match -- would still be caught
# via a wrong group span.


# two independent capturing quantifiers back to back -- each group's span must reflect its own greedy choice, at and around the joint minimum (4).
pattern (a{2,3})(b{2,3})
m "aabb" 0 4
g 1 0 2
g 2 2 4
m "aaabbb" 0 6
g 1 0 3
g 2 3 6
m "aabbb" 0 5
g 1 0 2
g 2 2 5
m "aaabb" 0 5
g 1 0 3
g 2 3 5
n "ab"

# alternation with a capture group PER branch: the branch not taken must report RX_UNSET (-1,-1), not a stale or zero span. Exercises the SMALLER branch (y, group 2) as the common case near the minimum.
pattern (?:(x{2,3})|(y))z
m "xxz" 0 3
g 1 0 2
g 2 -1 -1
m "xxxz" 0 4
g 1 0 3
g 2 -1 -1
m "yz" 0 2
g 1 -1 -1
g 2 0 1

# doubly-nested capturing groups around the SAME repeated quantifier: group 1 (outer) and group 2 (inner) both track the LAST iteration and must agree with each other, at the granularity boundaries family 4 already found (N=10 slides the match start).
pattern ((a{2,3})){2,3}c
m "aaaac" 0 5
g 1 2 4
g 2 2 4
m "aaaaac" 0 6
g 1 3 5
g 2 3 5
m "aaaaaaaaac" 0 10
g 1 6 9
g 2 6 9
m "aaaaaaaaaac" 1 11
g 1 7 10
g 2 7 10
